id=a52sxq_hwui_vulkan_default
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: UN1CA Vulkan renderer toggle (OpenGL default)
author=kusti420
description=The A52s vendor sets ro.hwui.use_vulkan empty, so every app rendered with OpenGL (skiagl); on the Fold8-based builds of early October that path showed green tile artifacts in Instagram/Facebook videos, which testers reported gone with Vulkan (not reproduced on 9.3.70 with OpenGL + V@0530: Instagram Reels now decodes AV1 in-app with dav1d, and a TextureView/SurfaceView matrix of H.264/HEVC/VP9/AV1, 8/10-bit, HDR10/HLG, hardware and software decoders showed none, 2026-10-22). Default the UN1CA Vulkan toggle to on (ro.hwui.use_vulkan stays unset so the toggle stays visible); an rc makes the toggle set skiavk or skiagl so turning it off still works. SurfaceFlinger RenderEngine is left at its default. 2026-10-21: the default is OpenGL again (owner decision, with the stock V@0530 driver as default); the toggle still switches both ways.
